<title>FRANCE: French Mar unemployment falls 4,800, rate 12.8 pct.</title>
<headline>French Mar unemployment falls 4,800, rate 12.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The seasonally adjusted number of people unemployed in France in March fell by 4,800, or 0.2 percent, to 3,087,500, labour ministry data showed.</p>
<p>The jobless rate, based on International Labour Organisation (ILO) criteria, which exclude jobseekers who did any work, was unchanged at a record 12.8 percent.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following seasonally adjusted data:</p>
<p>				  end-March month-on-month year-on-year</p>
<p> Jobless rate (ILO)	 12.8 pct   0.0 pctge pt   0.5 pctge pt</p>
<p> Unemployment		3,087,500    -0.2 pct	    2.2 pct</p>
<p> Unemployment (ILO)	3,282,000     0.2 pct	    4.6 pct</p>
<p> Jobs offered		  203,400     1.9 pct	    7.3 pct</p>
<p> New jobless registrations 366,600    -1.0 pct	   -4.4 pct</p>
<p> Jobless register exits    353,600    -0.3 pct	   -1.7 pct</p>
<p> Men under 25		  272,500    -1.8 pct	  -1.0 pct</p>
<p> Women under 25		313,000    -0.9 pct	  -3.0 pct</p>
<p> Men between 25 and 49   1,038,100    -0.2 pct	   3.2 pct</p>
<p> Women between 25 and 49 1,067,900     0.3 pct	   1.6 pct</p>
<p> Men 50 and over	     226,200     0.4 pct	   7.7 pct</p>
<p> Women 50 and over	   169,800     0.7 pct	   8.8 pct</p>
<p> Forced redundancy	    27,100    -1.1 pct	  -3.9 pct</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
</text>
